      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If your toddler is showing signs of dehydration, it's essential to contact your pediatrician first, but if you need immediate relief, you can try rehydrating him with small sips of a rehydration solution (such as Pedialyte) or offering him a splash of diluted water with a pinch of salt (about ¼ teaspoon for every 8 ounces) while constantly offering sips. Ensure he continues to drink and monitor for any worsening symptoms. Always consult with a healthcare provider before administering any treatment.",
