      "content": "It's very important not to give your child adult salt tablets as they are not designed for children and can be harmful. Only rehydration solutions or pediatric electrolyte drinks are safe to give for rehydration purposes. If he's not drinking enough, try to offer him his favorite fruits or vegetables that may contain natural electrolytes, like bananas, carrots, or cucumber. Dizziness can also be a sign of dehydration or an electrolyte imbalance, so if his symptoms continue or he shows signs of worsening, please seek advice from a healthcare professional immediately. Remember, giving adult medication to your child can be dangerous, and seeking a doctor’s advice is always the best course of action.",
